  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **The Night Time Is The Right Time** (1 other source): This track features John Scofield, Nigel Hall and Luther Dickinson all joining the band [1]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Soulive 2-29-12 set1 t01**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **Soulive 2-29-12 set1 t02**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **Soulive 2-29-12 set1 t03**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **Soulive 2-29-12 set1 t04**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **Soulive 2-29-12 set1 t05**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **Soulive 2-29-12 set1 t06**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **Soulive 2-29-12 set1 t07**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **Soulive 2-29-12 set1 t08**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **soulive2012-02-29.140s.flac16** (recommended): source not stated; 17 songs; 161 min [1]\n- **soulive2012-02-29.mk21.flac24**: audience recording; 14 songs; 162 min [2]\n- **soulive2012-02-29.mk21.flac16**: audience recording; 14 songs; 162 min [3]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Luther Dickinson plays throughout the whole of set two [1]\n- Guests include John Scofield on guitar, Nigel Hall on moog and/or vocals, and Luther Dickinson on guitar and vocals [2]\n- Guests include John Scofield on guitar, Nigel Hall on moog and/or vocals, and Luther Dickinson on guitar and vocals [3]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **soulive2012-02-29.140s.flac16**: taped by Frank D'Auria; transferred by Frank D'Auria; source: Neumann SKM 140's -> Edirol R44 [1]\n- **soulive2012-02-29.mk21.flac24**: taped by Eric McRoberts; transferred by Eric McRoberts; source: Audience/On Stage [2]. Also: This is a 24-bit version of the mk21 recording, not meant for MP3 streaming or CD burning [2]\n- **soulive2012-02-29.mk21.flac16**: taped by Eric McRoberts; transferred by Eric McRoberts; source: Audience/On Stage [3]. Also: This is the 16-bit version of the mk21 recording; a higher-quality 24-bit version also exists [3]",
